                        "glosses": [
                            "The last tetrachord, in the case where two tetrachords were placed separately from each other, but with only the interval of a tone between them."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c9ed0ed8-a547-45d8-8bf6-a95da29bae14",
                                "sense_id": "eecce6ba-ee8d-30cd-b05e-33c4610f9ad0",
                                "text": "1914, Vitruvius (translated by Morris Hicky Morgan), Ten Books on Architecture\nIn the middle range, place first at the extreme ends the vessels which give the note of the chromatic hyperbolaeon; next to them, those which give the chromatic diezeugmenon, a fourth below; third, the chromatic synhemmenon; fourth, the chromatic meson, a fourth below; fifth, the chromatic hypaton, a fourth below; sixth, the paramese, for this is both the concord of the fifth to the chromatic hyperbolaeon, and the concord of the chro­matic synhemmenon."
                            }
                        ]
